    {
      "_id": "5rJHfjHMwEkphQw2",
      "_key": "!actors.items!qsKgRb044u2EsI7y.5rJHfjHMwEkphQw2",
      "name": "Lair: Hungering Mire",
      "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-carved-stone-green.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "sort": 900,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "flags": {},
      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><em>Initiative 20 (loses ties). Additional XP 450.</em></p><p><strong>Regional Traits</strong></p><p><strong>Infested Water.</strong> Fumes coming off the grub-filled water prevent wounds from closing quickly. Creatures in the lair other than Growlbear can't use Hit Dice to regain Hit Points during a Short Rest.</p><p><strong>Shallow Traps.</strong> Hazardous traps lie hidden in the muck. A creature that spends 1 hour traveling in the lair or that fails an ability check to navigate the lair is subject to the following effect. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 14 Dexterity. <em>Failure:</em> 13 (3d8) Piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Lair Actions</strong> <em>(The lair can't take the same action two rounds in a row.)</em></p><p><strong>Swallybogs.</strong> Two Swallybogs emerge from the muck in unoccupied spaces of the lair's choice within the lair. They are Friendly to Growlbear and take their turns immediately after the lair.</p><p><strong>Spring Trap.</strong> A trap goes off in the mire. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 14 Dexterity, one creature of the lair's choice within the lair. <em>Failure:</em> 13 (3d8) Piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Monster Mist.</strong> A patch of sickening mist appears within the lair in a 30-foot-radius Sphere until the start of the lair's next turn. The area is Lightly Obscured. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 14 Constitution, each creature that starts its turn in the area other than Growlbear or a swallybog. <em>Failure:</em> The target is transformed into an amphibious hybrid. A transformed creature gains a Swim Speed of 15 feet and has Disadvantage on Charisma checks. The transformation lasts until the creature is targeted by a <em>Lesser Restoration</em> spell or similar magic.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
